00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:07.740
So how do I track what is
happening to my containers,

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:10.707
and who has access to
them-- changes, et cetera?

00:24:10.707 --> 00:24:12.790
MARK MANDEL: Yeah-- that's
a really good question.

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:14.498
If people aren't
aware-- on Google Cloud,

00:24:14.498 --> 00:24:17.220
there is a thing called
Cloud Audit Logging.

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:19.590
Cloud Audit Logging is
essentially set up to answer

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:22.428
that question of who did
what, where, and when.

00:24:22.428 --> 00:24:23.220
And that's a thing.

00:24:23.220 --> 00:24:25.320
And part of Cloud
Audit Logging is

00:24:25.320 --> 00:24:28.630
being able to do audit logging
on your containers as well.

00:24:28.630 --> 00:24:31.530
So by default, container
analysis-- audit logging

00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:35.700
is set up for admin activity--
so basically, anything an admin

00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:37.500
would do to any of
your containers.

00:24:37.500 --> 00:24:40.800
But for example-- container
analysis rights and things like

00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:41.940
that-- and reads--

00:24:41.940 --> 00:24:44.170
are not necessarily
set up by default.

00:24:44.170 --> 00:24:45.490
But you can set those up.

00:24:45.490 --> 00:24:48.540
So if you're go into
your Cloud Console

00:24:48.540 --> 00:24:50.820
and you go into Configuring
Data Access Logs,

00:24:50.820 --> 00:24:52.560
you're able to configure
exactly what it

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:55.290
is that you want to track
with your audit logs,

00:24:55.290 --> 00:24:57.983
regarding your containers--
maybe other audit logs as well.

00:24:57.983 --> 00:25:00.400
So you can see exactly what's
going on inside your system,

00:25:00.400 --> 00:25:01.950
if you want to track
certain security things

00:25:01.950 --> 00:25:03.780
or maybe just see what's
actually happening or maybe

00:25:03.780 --> 00:25:04.740
even debug a problem.

00:25:04.740 --> 00:25:06.930
So super, super handy
thing-- so if you ever

00:25:06.930 --> 00:25:08.770
need to see who
does what, where,

00:25:08.770 --> 00:25:11.260
and when to your containers,
you are able to do so.

